own prevented data collection in October 2025, so we are unable to measure the change. The Wage Growth Tracker will resume with the release of November data.\nL46: # Wage Growth Tracker\nL47: \nL48: The Atlanta Fed's Wage Growth Tracker is a measure of the nominal wage growth of individuals. It is constructed using microdata from the Current Population Survey (CPS), and is the median percent change in the hourly wage of individuals observed 12 months apart. Our measure is based on methodology developed by colleagues at the San Francisco Fed.\nL49: \nL50: 【39†Subscribe to Email Updates Subscribe to Email Updates】\nL51: \nL52: 【40†Image: Center for Human Capital Studies' Wage Growth Tracker】\nL53: \nL54: Close\nL55: \nL56: ﻿\nL57: ## Enter your information\nL58: \nL59: First name *\nL60: [Input]\nL61: \nL62: Last name *\nL63: [Input]\nL64: \nL65: Email *\nL66: [Input]\nL67: \nL68: Message *\nL69: [Input]\nL70: \nL71: * Required field\nL72: \nL73: [Input]\nL74: \nL75: [Input] [Input] [Input]\nL76: ## 3.9%\nL77: \nL78: Wage Growth Tracker (3-month overall unweighted, September 2026)\nL79: \nL80: October 2026\nL81: \nL82: The Atlanta Fed's Wage Growth Tracker is a measure of the nominal wage growth of individuals. It is constructed using microdata from the Current Population Survey (CPS), and is the median percent change in the hourly wage of individuals observed 12 months apart. Our measure is based on methodology developed by colleagues at the San Francisco Fed.\nL83: \nL84: Updated: October 08, 2026\nL85:   * [Button: Interactive Chart ]\nL86:   * [Button: Methodology ]\nL87:   * [Button: Data Distribution ]\nL88:   * [Button: Related Links ]\nL89: \nL90: Show Filters\nL91: \nL92: Filters\nL93: \nL94: Moving Average\nL95: \nL96: [Button: 3-Month] [Button: 12-Month] Job Characteristic\nL97: \nL98: [Input] Stayer/Switcher\nL99: \nL100: [Input] Industry\nL101: \nL102: [Input] Full-Time\nL103: \nL104: [Input] Hourly/Weekly Basis\nL105: \nL106: [Input] Wage Distribution\nL